# First-run environment template for stellar-agent-guard-dashboard.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and uncomment only what you need:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Every value below already has a safe default in `lib/guard/network.ts`, so an
# empty copy is a working public-testnet console. `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values are
# inlined by Next at build time, so restart `npm run dev` after changing one.
# Never put a real secret in this file or in `.env.local`: the console is a
# non-custodial client and never needs an admin key to read or sign.

# ── Network the console reads and broadcasts to ──────────────────────────────
# Default: https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RPC_URL=https://soroban-testnet.stellar.org
# Default: Test SDF Network ; September 2015
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK_PASSPHRASE=Test SDF Network ; September 2015
# Default: testnet (shown in the wallet-mismatch message)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK_NAME=testnet

# ── Guard the selector opens on ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Default: the Phase 1 guard, `PHASE1_ARTIFACT.guard` in lib/guard/network.ts.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GUARD_CONTRACT_ID=C...
# The instance the pinned artifact bytes are verified against before a deploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARTIFACT_SOURCE_CONTRACT_ID=C...

# ── Demo mode (no RPC, no wallet, writes disabled) ───────────────────────────
# `npm run dev:demo` sets this for you; `?demo=true` does the same per visit.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=true

# ── Local sandbox only ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `npm run sandbox` writes these into `.env.local` for the throwaway local
# network. They are test-only keys: never fund them and never reuse them on
# another network.
# SAG_LOCAL_ADMIN_SECRET=S...
# SAG_LOCAL_AGENT_SECRET=S...
